      <div class="accordion faq-accordion" id="faqAccordion">
        
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading1">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse1" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse1">
              What is the step-by-step process for private limited company registration in Jaipur in 2025?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="collapse1" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading1" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <p class='speakable-answer'>The process for registering a private limited company in Jaipur involves obtaining a Digital Signature Certificate (DSC), reserving a unique company name, and filing the SPICe+ form with the Registrar of Companies (ROC) for Kanpur, which has jurisdiction over Jaipur.</p>\n\n**Here is a more detailed breakdown of the steps:**\n* **Step 1: Obtain DSC and DIN:** Get a Digital Signature Certificate (DSC) and Director Identification Number (DIN) for all proposed directors.\n* **Step 2: Reserve Company Name:** Apply for name reservation using the RUN service on the MCA portal.\n* **Step 3: Draft MoA and AoA:** Draft the Memorandum of Association (MoA) and Articles of Association (AoA).\n* **Step 4: File SPICe+ Form:** File the integrated SPICe+ form on the MCA portal.\n* **Step 5: Pay Stamp Duty:** Pay the required stamp duty as per Rajasthan's regulations.\n* **Step 6: Obtain Certificate of Incorporation:** Once approved, you will receive the Certificate of Incorporation (COI), PAN, and TAN.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading2">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse2">
              How much does it cost to register a trademark in Delhi?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="collapse2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading2" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <p class='speakable-answer'>The cost of trademark registration in Delhi varies. For an individual or a startup, the government fee is ₹4,500 per class. For companies, it's ₹9,000 per class. Professional fees for expert assistance are additional.</p>\n\n**Here is a simple cost breakdown:**\n* **Government Fees:**\n  * Individual/Startup: ₹4,500 per class.\n  * Company/LLP: ₹9,000 per class.\n* **Professional Fees:** These can range from ₹2,000 to ₹10,000.\n* **Total Estimated Cost:** For a startup, the total cost is typically between ₹6,500 and ₹14,500.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading3">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse3">
              What documents are required for GST registration for a sole proprietorship in Mumbai?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="collapse3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading3" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <p class='speakable-answer'>For a sole proprietorship in Mumbai, the main documents for GST registration are the owner's PAN card, Aadhar card, a photograph, proof of business address (like a rent agreement and electricity bill), and a bank account statement.</p>\n\n**Here is a checklist of the required documents:**\n* **Identity Proof:** PAN card of the proprietor.\n* **Address Proof:** Aadhar card or passport.\n* **Photograph:** A recent passport-size photograph.\n* **Business Address Proof:** A recent utility bill and either a property tax receipt (if owned) or a rent agreement and NOC (if rented).\n* **Bank Account Proof:** A copy of a cancelled cheque or bank passbook.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading4">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse4">
              What is the best way to get an employment visa in Bengaluru for a foreign national?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="collapse4" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading4" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <p class='speakable-answer'>The best way to get an employment visa in Bengaluru is to work with an experienced immigration consultant. They can help you prepare the correct documents, including the employment contract, and guide you through the application process with the Indian consulate and the FRRO registration in Bengaluru.</p>\n\n**Here is a simplified process:**\n1. **Engage a Consultant:** Find a reputable immigration consultant in Bengaluru.\n2. **Gather Documents:** You will need a valid passport, a signed employment contract, and proof of your qualifications.\n3. **Apply at Consulate:** The initial visa application is made at the Indian embassy in your country of residence.\n4. **FRRO Registration:** After arriving in India, you must register with the FRRO in Bengaluru within 14 days.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading5">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse5" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse5">
              Which ROC has jurisdiction for companies registered in Jaipur?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="collapse5" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading5" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <p class='speakable-answer'>Companies registered in Jaipur fall under the jurisdiction of the Registrar of Companies (ROC), Kanpur. Even though Jaipur is in Rajasthan, the administrative office for company law matters is in Kanpur, Uttar Pradesh. All filings and communications will be with ROC Kanpur.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading6">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse6" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse6">
              Are there any specific local licenses required to start a tourism business in Dehradun?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="collapse6" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading6" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <p class='speakable-answer'>Yes, to start a tourism business in Dehradun, in addition to your company registration, you will likely need a license from the Uttarakhand Tourism Development Board (UTDB). Depending on your specific services (e.g., hotel, travel agency, adventure sports), other permits may be required.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading7">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse7" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse7">
              How long does it take to get an FSSAI license in India in 2025?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="collapse7" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading7" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <p class='speakable-answer'>The time it takes to get an FSSAI license in India depends on the type of license. A basic registration can be obtained in 7-10 days, while a state or central license can take 30-60 days, assuming all documents are correct.</p>\n\n* **Basic Registration:** 7-10 working days.\n* **State License:** 30-45 working days.\n* **Central License:** 50-60 working days.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading8">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse8" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse8">
              What is the difference between a Director and a Shareholder?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="collapse8" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading8" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <p class='speakable-answer'>A Director is responsible for managing the company's day-to-day affairs, while a Shareholder is an owner of the company. A person can be both a director and a shareholder.</p>\n\n* **Director:** Appointed by shareholders to manage the company.\n* **Shareholder:** Owns shares in the company, representing ownership.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading9">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse9" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse9">
              Can a foreign national be a director in an Indian company?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="collapse9" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading9" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <p class='speakable-answer'>Yes, a foreign national can be a director in an Indian company. However, the company must have at least one director who is a resident of India. The foreign director will need to obtain a Director Identification Number (DIN).</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading10">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse10" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse10">
              How do I choose the right business structure for my startup?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="collapse10" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading10" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <p class='speakable-answer'>Choosing the right business structure depends on factors like the number of owners, liability protection, and funding requirements. A Private Limited Company is best for startups looking for funding and limited liability, while an LLP is good for professional firms. A Sole Proprietorship is the simplest for a single owner.</p>\n\n* **Private Limited Company:** For startups that plan to raise funds.\n* **LLP:** For professional service providers.\n* **One Person Company (OPC):** For solo entrepreneurs who want limited liability.\n* **Sole Proprietorship:** For small businesses with a single owner.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading11">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse11" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse11">
              What is a 'speakable' schema and how does it help with voice search?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="collapse11" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading11" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <p class='speakable-answer'>'Speakable' schema is a type of structured data that you can add to your website to identify content that is well-suited for being read aloud by voice assistants like Google Assistant. It helps voice search technology to deliver more natural and accurate answers.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading12">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse12" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse12">
              How can I make my website's FAQ page AI-friendly?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="collapse12" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading12" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <p class='speakable-answer'>To make your FAQ page AI-friendly, use clear and concise language, structure your content with headings and bullet points, use Q&A and HowTo schema, and answer questions directly. AI assistants prefer content that is easy to parse and understand.</p>\n\n* **Use clear headings.**\n* **Write in simple sentences.**\n* **Use bullet points and numbered lists.**\n* **Implement FAQPage, QAPage, and HowTo schema.**\n* **Answer the question directly in the first sentence.**
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading13">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse13" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse13">
              What are the annual compliances for a private limited company in India?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="collapse13" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading13" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <p class='speakable-answer'>The main annual compliances for a private limited company in India include filing an annual return with the ROC (Form MGT-7), filing financial statements (Form AOC-4), holding an Annual General Meeting (AGM), and filing income tax returns.</p>\n\n* **Form MGT-7:** Annual Return.\n* **Form AOC-4:** Financial Statements.\n* **Annual General Meeting (AGM):** Must be held within 6 months of the end of the financial year.\n* **Income Tax Return:** Must be filed by the due date.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading14">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse14" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse14">
              Can I register a company with a residential address in India?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="collapse14" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading14" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <p class='speakable-answer'>Yes, you can register a company with a residential address in India. You will need to provide proof of address, such as a utility bill, and a No Objection Certificate (NOC) from the owner of the property.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading15">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse15" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse15">
              How do I protect my brand name in India?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="collapse15" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading15" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <p class='speakable-answer'>The best way to protect your brand name in India is by registering it as a trademark. A trademark gives you the exclusive right to use your brand name for the goods or services you offer, and it prevents others from using a similar name.</p>\n\n* **Conduct a Trademark Search:** To ensure your name is unique.\n* **File a Trademark Application:** With the Indian Trademark Registry.\n* **Respond to Objections:** If any are raised by the examiner.\n* **Get the Registration Certificate:** Once approved.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading16">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse16" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse16">
              What is the difference between an LLP and a Private Limited Company?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="collapse16" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading16" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <p class='speakable-answer'>An LLP (Limited Liability Partnership) has lower compliance requirements and is easier to manage, making it ideal for professional firms. A Private Limited Company is more suitable for startups that intend to raise external funding, as it allows for equity-based investments.</p>\n\n* **LLP:** Lower compliance, flexible structure.\n* **Private Limited Company:** Easier to raise funds, more structured governance.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading17">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse17" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse17">
              How can I check if a company name is available?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="collapse17" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading17" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <p class='speakable-answer'>You can check if a company name is available by using the 'Check Company Name' service on the Ministry of Corporate Affairs (MCA) portal. It's important to choose a unique name that is not similar to any existing company or trademark to avoid rejection.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading18">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse18" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse18">
              What is a Director Identification Number (DIN)?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="collapse18" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading18" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <p class='speakable-answer'>A Director Identification Number (DIN) is a unique 8-digit number required for any person who wants to be a director of a company in India. It is issued by the Ministry of Corporate Affairs and is valid for the lifetime of the director.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading19">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse19" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse19">
              What is the penalty for not filing annual returns for a company?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="collapse19" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading19" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <p class='speakable-answer'>The penalty for not filing annual returns on time can be significant. The Companies Act, 2013 imposes a penalty of ₹100 per day for each form that is not filed, with no upper limit. This can lead to heavy fines and the company being struck off by the ROC.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading20">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse20" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse20">
              Do I need a physical office to register a company in India?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="collapse20" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading20" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <p class='speakable-answer'>While you don't need a commercial office, you must have a registered office address in India that is capable of receiving official communications. This can be a residential address, provided you have a No Objection Certificate (NOC) from the owner.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading21">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse21" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse21">
              How can a startup get recognized under the Startup India program?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="collapse21" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading21" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <p class='speakable-answer'>To get recognized under the Startup India program, your business must be a new entity (less than 10 years old), have an annual turnover of less than ₹100 crore, and be working towards innovation, development, or improvement of products or services. You can apply for recognition on the Startup India portal.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading22">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse22" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse22">
              What is a 'Shareholder Agreement' and why is it important?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="collapse22" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading22" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <p class='speakable-answer'>A Shareholder Agreement is a contract between the shareholders of a company that outlines their rights, responsibilities, and the rules for managing the company. It is important because it helps to prevent disputes between shareholders and provides a clear framework for decision-making.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading23">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse23" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse23">
              What is FEMA compliance for a company?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="collapse23" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading23" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <p class='speakable-answer'>FEMA (Foreign Exchange Management Act) compliance is a set of rules and regulations that govern foreign exchange transactions in India. For a company, this includes reporting foreign investments (FDI), overseas investments (ODI), and other foreign transactions to the Reserve Bank of India (RBI).</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading24">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse24" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse24">
              How can I get a work permit for a foreign employee in India?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="collapse24" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading24" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <p class='speakable-answer'>To get a work permit (Employment Visa) for a foreign employee, the Indian employer needs to provide an employment contract that meets the minimum salary requirements (currently over $25,000 USD per annum). The foreign national must then apply for the Employment Visa at the Indian consulate in their home country.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading25">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse25" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse25">
              What is the difference between GST Registration and GST Return Filing?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="collapse25" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading25" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <p class='speakable-answer'>GST Registration is the process of obtaining a unique Goods and Services Tax Identification Number (GSTIN) for your business. GST Return Filing is the process of submitting periodic reports to the tax authorities detailing your sales, purchases, and GST liability.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
      </div>
